ss preparation, exhibits, motions, and negotiation strategy."}]}, {"id": "d949ed02-820c-4f85-b07c-86027c2a01e2", "type": "topic", "title": "Trial Process and Adversarial Procedure", "description": "Understand the structure, rights, tactics, and institutional purpose of American criminal trials.", "children": [{"id": "51d71fae-2cbf-4d9e-ac5e-58b14af97c67", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Anatomy of a trial", "children": [{"id": "c08ffdb9-a437-4972-8215-081f1d13b184", "type": "concept", "title": "Opening statements"}, {"id": "65d37b99-133c-4510-be0a-00dd5e4bd7a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Direct examination"}, {"id": "02f34b9f-a56e-4a01-9ff4-22b84e0b2928", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-examination"}, {"id": "a171379f-c01a-440c-a8be-54d07a401b0e", "type": "concept", "title": "Closing arguments"}], "description": "Trial process shows how adversarial proof becomes a public judgment."}, {"id": "74a30620-4568-4d39-819d-5923f23f90e9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Trial rights", "children": [{"id": "7258c310-d4d6-4a36-8d78-862d3a2e7f39", "type": "concept", "title": "Confrontation"}, {"id": "90aac2b8-b431-4f43-87ee-95765b72d377", "type": "concept", "title": "Compulsory process"}, {"id": "23fa15f8-5236-4eee-8b4a-de2d3aaa9a60", "type": "concept", "title": "Right to jury"}, {"id": "c2d918aa-f6fa-4b22-86ef-ff9e1bdde3a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Burden of proof"}], "description": "Criminal trials embody constitutional commitments to confrontation, compulsory process, jury trial, and proof beyond reasonable doubt."}, {"id": "1d72e4de-33b1-4b8e-8481-f83071516608", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Judicial control of trial", "children": [{"id": "07164791-15b1-420f-a5a8-5803ef9be76e", "type": "concept", "title": "Objections"}, {"id": "75c8ebd5-5472-4e11-ac14-41092362b7ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Sidebars"}, {"id": "ddab1f7f-58da-47ff-8cda-51e5cc3125d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Motions for judgment"}, {"id": "b2fafd5d-1683-4547-84bc-3880c26ade3d", "type": "concept", "title": "Jury instructions"}], "description": "Judges manage admissibility, procedure, jury instructions, decorum, and the record."}]}, {"id": "8c7f8adb-7947-4c14-b9d2-973ab17c8752", "type": "topic", "title": "Jury Selection, Deliberation, and Verdicts", "description": "Study juries as democratic factfinders shaped by selection rules, deliberation dynamics, instructions, and verdict forms.", "children": [{"id": "4d3c6646-108c-48dc-9f86-4dc99cc0cfed", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Jury pool and voir dire", "children": [{"id": "6b693ef9-2f70-4fa8-8603-8485f9200bfb", "type": "concept", "title": "Jury source lists"}, {"id": "4f04ba18-c8df-465c-8e72-379b8c39981d", "type": "concept", "title": "Voir dire"}, {"id": "13886f65-7a8f-4ee5-80a1-83ff633ebeac", "type": "concept", "title": "Challenges for cause"}, {"id": "7c5878b8-4389-45ed-9c09-3469e7b2bbf4", "type": "concept", "title": "Peremptory challenges"}], "description": "Jury selection determines who will judge facts and whether bias can be identified."}, {"id": "a9df9c70-a73b-40ee-8dff-7a4cb7565888", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Deliberation and decision-making", "children": [{"id": "03c98047-6f52-4016-99f4-ad63fca869d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Foreperson role"}, {"id": "20e54082-4302-43f2-8f5e-f3004f76da15", "type": "concept", "title": "Unanimity rules"}, {"id": "a8c2e0a4-8dd6-4451-8d66-1fbaa810e978", "type": "concept", "title": "Jury instructions"}, {"id": "9473756e-60dd-4534-8139-d9b95079f1f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Deadlock and Allen charges"}], "description": "Jury deliberation blends law, evidence, group dynamics, memory, and instructions."}, {"id": "290b8544-6b4b-4bb6-a54b-baf5982793f9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Verdicts and legitimacy", "children": [{"id": "b99d2dd2-abec-4168-99d7-28fff492f122", "type": "concept", "title": "General verdicts"}, {"id": "559bf5ee-5a75-47e3-b078-2ee7dd524ab0", "type": "concept", "title": "Special findings awareness"}, {"id": "84475c11-00de-452c-8a51-c5921d36854f", "type": "concept", "title": "Hung juries"}, {"id": "dbabe0ff-78c0-4821-bd9b-d9b5dba41b46", "type": "concept", "title": "Public confidence"}], "description": "Verdicts carry legal force and public meaning, especially in high-stakes criminal cases."}]}, {"id": "3f5e139a-101b-40a4-8a66-87e670e4c8bf", "type": "topic", "title": "Sentencing Law, Guidelines, and Punishment Purposes", "description": "Analyze how courts impose punishment and how law, discretion, risk, and policy shape sentences.", "children": [{"id": "748ab275-055c-4024-a3d4-ca7a093c4d0d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Purposes of punishment", "children": [{"id": "866727c9-9eda-4e38-a119-af83bed642e0", "type": "concept", "title": "Retribution"}, {"id": "e8924874-567a-4def-9812-dd3906195230", "type": "concept", "title": "Deterrence"}, {"id": "f0e7c1bd-6116-4b60-965c-8b0d0e9495d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Incapacitation"}, {"id": "bae1a942-06e0-4721-872c-752999070e11", "type": "concept", "title": "Rehabilitation and restoration"}], "description": "Sentencing reflects contested ideas about what punishment is for."}, {"id": "7c9cfd67-302c-41be-ab88-e2db375b1db1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sentencing structures", "children": [{"id": "bc6d7281-c95d-4d64-baea-366600fba0c1", "type": "concept", "title": "Guidelines"}, {"id": "2aecc836-c7f9-443a-a2c5-4b06ff528582", "type": "concept", "title": "Mandatory minimums"}, {"id": "9137286f-ac11-4c2c-9581-0f331f6a6a1f", "type": "concept", "title": "Presentence reports"}, {"id": "c1d7f8b2-38da-495e-8469-5f94bf811a3e", "type": "concept", "title": "Judicial discretion"}], "description": "American sentencing varies across guidelines, mandatory minimums, discretion, and negotiated outcomes."}, {"id": "42777ba4-e339-46c9-8617-00e7ae95a5b0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Collateral consequences and reentry", "children": [{"id": "95922693-ebcf-4971-9fed-24c5eb424742", "type": "concept", "title": "Fines and fees"}, {"id": "078c1ef8-3455-4cb4-a897-489e8917c3e1", "type": "concept", "title": "Probation conditions"}, {"id": "67089b53-14cf-45d6-83ea-ed78fcc36745", "type": "concept", "title": "Collateral consequences"}, {"id": "c31dec49-0c20-40ea-b743-0169a2c5938a", "type": "concept", "title": "Reentry barriers"}], "description": "Sentences extend beyond the courtroom into housing, employment, family life, and civic participation."}]}, {"id": "cffb4802-77b4-47b5-8547-d2d6d459ea80", "type": "topic", "title": "Appeals, Post-Conviction Review, and Habeas", "description": "Trace how legal errors, constitutional claims, and wrongful convictions are reviewed after judgment.", "children": [{"id": "ba02abef-d058-4f61-8684-f73558765667", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Direct appeals", "children": [{"id": "bd6feee0-03ba-4ecc-8392-963320a18ea9", "type": "concept", "title": "Notice of appeal"}, {"id": "302f038a-3812-401d-9e5f-832c81131f30", "type": "concept", "title": "Standards of review"}, {"id": "6ba0788e-7542-43cd-b932-c837f349e57c", "type": "concept", "title": "Harmless error"}, {"id": "094fdbf0-8972-4eab-b685-c5f300b37185", "type": "concept", "title": "Appellate briefs and oral argument"}], "description": "Appeals review legal error rather than retry facts from scratch."}, {"id": "c47c065f-913e-4745-9400-376693a20983", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Post-conviction remedies", "children": [{"id": "37d14602-9f7f-4c68-98cc-58902d229bf4", "type": "concept", "title": "Ineffective assistance"}, {"id": "0611fff0-0ce2-416c-8b14-347103e75e12", "type": "concept", "title": "New evidence"}, {"id": "26f0eeee-1a57-42d4-8c43-ce32d728a69b", "type": "concept", "title": "State post-conviction petitions"}, {"id": "47aa07bf-cd08-4def-8f25-b048419bc8af", "type": "concept", "title": "Federal habeas overview"}], "description": "Post-conviction review addresses claims that often require facts outside the trial record."}, {"id": "cf059b01-da53-47cc-afb8-d1b445537147", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Wrongful convictions", "children": [{"id": "252248ee-e25e-479c-9a9c-07b30dea77d0", "type": "concept", "title": "DNA evidence"}, {"id": "b4a32397-f5e5-4448-bb6b-8983de26bf6d", "type": "concept", "title": "False confessions"}, {"id": "c1616db9-9bea-4626-99e5-38bb4a5ca4c7", "type": "concept", "title": "Eyewitness error"}, {"id": "68542c1d-73c2-49a0-bef3-68b9a1c4452a", "type": "concept", "title": "Official misconduct"}], "description": "The review system reveals both safeguards and limits in correcting miscarriages of justice."}]}, {"id": "c3ab9a97-cbd9-4be5-a0c2-43239adfaecf", "type": "topic", "title": "Specialized and Problem-Solving Courts", "description": "Evaluate drug courts, mental health courts, veterans courts, juvenile courts, and other specialized adjudication models.", "children": [{"id": "9c49f195-0ec7-47ca-b0ca-9c3f33b13dff", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Drug and treatment courts", "children": [{"id": "91a44fc3-86dc-46fe-8fd5-828cc9a3e871", "type": "concept", "title": "Drug courts"}, {"id": "be167c27-8e2f-419d-b512-326701e1bc17", "type": "concept", "title": "Mental health courts"}, {"id": "4da09883-a518-420a-b09a-f2cff46dd1be", "type": "concept", "title": "Treatment compliance"}, {"id": "58c607cb-18c3-455b-8b96-09a0ac971e6f", "type": "concept", "title": "Graduated sanctions"}], "description": "Problem-solving courts seek to address underlying needs while managing legal accountability."}, {"id": "37f1b980-e121-4df3-9f26-f75148caec10", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Juvenile and family-oriented courts", "children": [{"id": "c2b38da0-b8c2-4080-a07b-b0a668fd7136", "type": "concept", "title": "Juvenile court"}, {"id": "5974e4f8-f669-4f60-9450-a3ee1e150f48", "type": "concept", "title": "Family court intersections"}, {"id": "b1ae3e68-3ad2-4354-9afc-46ca19e21fc3", "type": "concept", "title": "Status offenses"}, {"id": "1638c546-5ddb-4465-b06d-e9302ccc318d", "type": "concept", "title": "Best interests and rehabilitation"}], "description": "Specialized courts often use different goals, procedures, and confidentiality norms."}, {"id": "2f895f49-a9a9-456f-af7c-e08621a2d84f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evaluation and critique", "children": [{"id": "2e35b88a-5e70-40cb-8bc2-1baa4719a953", "type": "concept", "title": "Recidivism evidence"}, {"id": "f41b7db2-517c-43bc-bd75-ffa817063ff5", "type": "concept", "title": "Eligibility and exclusion"}, {"id": "85cfa518-5ed2-464b-838b-3347aa9a2ab5", "type": "concept", "title": "Net widening"}, {"id": "1edf317a-1721-44bb-83ee-6eedcc3748cc", "type": "concept", "title": "Procedural justice"}], "description": "Students assess whether specialized courts improve outcomes or create new forms of coercion and inequality."}]}, {"id": "02c8a33d-a0b0-4d85-81e4-49b31968ce17", "type": "topic", "title": "Court Administration, Caseflow, and Judicial Performance", "description": "Study courts as organizations managing caseloads, budgets, delay, records, technology, and public accountability.", "children": [{"id": "afd2e089-d103-4f5d-a9d8-b5ed97f14dd5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Court management", "children": [{"id": "6b3e0b71-99a1-4fd3-8ef1-b75f52d357d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Calendaring"}, {"id": "ec0f7681-5713-4403-9928-caccea9b7a67", "type": "concept", "title": "Docket control"}, {"id": "73d5adc4-1f0d-4b46-af00-1d8fd35fd6c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Continuance policy"}, {"id": "1f0a2e7e-6774-4f6e-84e6-9890b19adfaa", "type": "concept", "title": "Court leadership"}], "description": "Courts are public organizations with budgets, staffing, calendars, facilities, and administrative constraints."}, {"id": "f1c5ea85-46c6-4c40-b494-51dee3d34333", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Performance measurement", "children": [{"id": "9184b8dd-733d-4425-a08c-7cb35a2eea57", "type": "concept", "title": "Caseload data"}, {"id": "86ba4d07-5ce0-4fc7-b442-4ba800971372", "type": "concept", "title": "Clearance rates"}, {"id": "d84a2af0-6c8e-4577-bbac-50c24c3f0472", "type": "concept", "title": "Time to disposition"}, {"id": "bb2f8096-2408-4aa5-a805-0a4c6e76363e", "type": "concept", "title": "Failure-to-appear metrics"}], "description": "Court statistics help evaluate access, timeliness, clearance rates, backlog, and fairness."}, {"id": "20d6bbd4-ce99-45dd-b354-7bdc79334e8e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Transparency and public accountability", "children": [{"id": "f06f90d1-6276-44f5-abc0-ce152ffa2a01", "type": "concept", "title": "Public records"}, {"id": "e65bbcac-6815-4134-b198-cebdfcd6fe26", "type": "concept", "title": "Open courts"}, {"id": "f7644a83-efd6-4dde-9f67-c96ffb22a6ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Media access"}, {"id": "61419b5d-55dc-4373-aaba-0772f2dd2439", "type": "concept", "title": "Plain-language court information"}], "description": "Court legitimacy depends partly on records, open proceedings, understandable processes, and public trust."}]}, {"id": "6332af15-fa2f-4738-917b-6f3e6bacbaeb", "type": "topic", "title": "Technology, Data, and Access to Justice", "description": "Examine e-filing, remote hearings, court data, AI risks, language access, self-represented litigants, and digital inequality.", "children": [{"id": "b84bde78-23e9-4885-87ca-867233ae7f85", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital court systems", "children": [{"id": "623f9051-f473-4148-84f7-0fef6ba4baba", "type": "concept", "title": "E-filing"}, {"id": "444c6ab6-c92f-49b3-a3cb-93de3ab46c47", "type": "concept", "title": "Online records"}, {"id": "ad28ef05-2eb7-4c90-bb7e-c1b9371abaa4", "type": "concept", "title": "Remote hearings"}, {"id": "ec6b9b2a-5c30-4624-9b7a-34170b9f8628", "type": "concept", "title": "Digital evidence systems"}], "description": "Technology changes how people file, appear, communicate, and access court information."}, {"id": "445cf8a6-9a63-48fc-97d5-cc63a387b722", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Access to justice", "children": [{"id": "6f7c0885-2b4e-492e-a603-3ef474446003", "type": "concept", "title": "Self-represented litigants"}, {"id": "13cba88c-84ae-4ff5-9055-4aa5a0579220", "type": "concept", "title": "Language access"}, {"id": "569d852c-8c88-4428-ab19-721712205199", "type": "concept", "title": "ADA access"}, {"id": "f59cee3d-7b7b-469c-9b04-bcaa43d9a1a6", "type": "concept", "title": "Legal aid"}], "description": "Court access depends on cost, counsel, language, disability accommodation, geography, and procedural complexity."}, {"id": "31e58d5b-7524-41da-b79a-6b2e79aad3a2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Algorithmic and data risks", "children": [{"id": "9039ab1b-1c96-4c0a-8d04-8124edf8875c", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk assessment"}, {"id": "cc46494e-be82-4713-b5be-81fdd115c0ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Data quality"}, {"id": "aa5f7376-fe3e-4575-95fb-d60b37a59457", "type": "concept", "title": "Explainability"}, {"id": "3a5080cc-3900-47c8-8b61-3e2c0da28995", "type": "concept", "title": "Audit and governance"}], "description": "Students evaluate how data tools can support courts while creating bias, opacity, or due process problems."}]}, {"id": "fd960e57-82d8-49e2-b823-6bc4180daa7d", "type": "topic", "title": "Inequality, Disparities, and Legitimacy in Courts", "description": "Confront how race, class, gender, geography, disability, and citizenship status affect court experiences and outcomes.", "children": [{"id": "830391c1-710b-41c0-b8ea-f11f6db8f3f2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Disparity across decision points", "children": [{"id": "047c757d-87b5-4983-9d56-772d894eb13e", "type": "concept", "title": "Race and ethnicity"}, {"id": "3f177ac9-d588-4d3b-8f71-3bb774d2f3bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Class and wealth"}, {"id": "0004dfd8-a46c-4c69-869f-1a600edb8708", "type": "concept", "title": "Gender and sexuality"}, {"id": "adf0ac67-cc4a-44fe-958b-c84c88006a77", "type": "concept", "title": "Geography"}], "description": "Inequality can enter at charging, bail, plea, trial, sentencing, and appeal."}, {"id": "49ba2ebd-a5cc-4166-a887-750efbf8b6e9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Procedural justice", "children": [{"id": "f9a9ea1a-4fc2-4792-8435-9bef331cfad5", "type": "concept", "title": "Voice"}, {"id": "ba66b6ea-b65f-4e7a-9336-f80e7169c81d", "type": "concept", "title": "Neutrality"}, {"id": "59d8072a-fad8-42ce-871e-c21dbdff2941", "type": "concept", "title": "Respect"}, {"id": "07507033-4bfc-45de-abaa-bfcb35bd5c71", "type": "concept", "title": "Trustworthy authority"}], "description": "People are more likely to see courts as legitimate when they experience voice, neutrality, respect, and trustworthy motives."}, {"id": "05ae0049-fd6d-4eb9-91fd-cb2bd3cc0c5f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reform and accountability", "children": [{"id": "547b5aa4-f64d-4f79-8d57-09c5f37e79cd", "type": "concept", "title": "Bail reform"}, {"id": "3ad995b5-3a46-42e2-b04f-2722bb3334aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Public defense reform"}, {"id": "9c3b0cb3-2465-49f1-91d6-32e3456d2c08", "type": "concept", "title": "Sentencing reform"}, {"id": "048f6522-31c5-4743-b1aa-e76e9660c6de", "type": "concept", "title": "Data transparency"}], "description": "Court reform requires diagnosing problems without flattening institutional complexity."}]}, {"id": "f41cf85a-b6a3-4efb-8c46-7bbc64183984", "type": "topic", "title": "Victims, Witnesses, and Community Participation", "description": "Understand how adjudication affects and depends on victims, witnesses, families, communities, and public trust.", "children": [{"id": "53c7ea09-ed05-4d97-a667-81a0a5fb6005", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Victim roles and rights", "children": [{"id": "ff19af78-4d2d-41bb-80fc-f422284a7f63", "type": "concept", "title": "Victim notification"}, {"id": "e2a6f8b1-83ab-4728-8741-d9aa5e0c0833", "type": "concept", "title": "Impact statements"}, {"id": "f1dd6195-9821-4df5-8df8-d513972433d2", "type": "concept", "title": "Restitution"}, {"id": "6f442eaa-030d-4a0a-a56f-5d1c7d53211a", "type": "concept", "title": "Confidentiality and safety"}], "description": "Victims may participate through notification, statements, restitution, and consultation, but criminal prosecution remains public."}, {"id": "9a1b8451-ad44-49b5-ab28-5100e0a441fb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Witness experience", "children": [{"id": "f5be03f4-a0d8-4266-9a2e-b29644835d7b", "type": "concept", "title": "Subpoenas"}, {"id": "88312fcd-7b50-4715-9c7a-1fc76607b12e", "type": "concept", "title": "Witness intimidation"}, {"id": "5d592e18-7274-4b62-8600-de7d3e3a5032", "type": "concept", "title": "Trauma-informed practice"}, {"id": "63e65353-8526-40f5-9234-4ff1755e814a", "type": "concept", "title": "Credibility assessment"}], "description": "Witnesses need protection, preparation, support, and fair treatment to make adjudication work."}, {"id": "efbe3667-f5c1-4506-84bd-3a290c9e961e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Community and public trust", "children": [{"id": "c1433bbf-0bc8-4ad6-9af7-70bc9efcb985", "type": "concept", "title": "Court observation"}, {"id": "2f33a2f3-dc97-4414-b8f1-dc2e312fb16d", "type": "concept", "title": "Community courts"}, {"id": "d7d98d1a-8b10-4ab3-bc09-36ec258df294", "type": "concept", "title": "Media coverage"}, {"id": "9bed2399-bcd8-49ac-8a93-76c83dd26887", "type": "concept", "title": "Public legal education"}], "description": "Courts serve communities, and community perceptions affect cooperation and legitimacy."}]}, {"id": "2b3bb0ab-e449-4c9b-bdfe-73ba1c892c92", "type": "topic", "title": "Court Observation, Policy Reform, and Capstone Analysis", "description": "Integrate doctrine, institutional analysis, data, and field observation into a practical courts reform memo or case study.", "children": [{"id": "1d52c0c6-b406-4fcc-b1e8-1a622991fe5f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Court observation methods", "children": [{"id": "47254bc5-577e-4ff0-b14d-fa469557ed2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Field notes"}, {"id": "f26ce5ef-b23a-42d7-a18d-ecc432627e1f", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethical observation"}, {"id": "67be27f6-b3ea-42d8-81b8-07ce6730702f", "type": "concept", "title": "Actor mapping"}, {"id": "ce9ea59f-9a4c-4bb0-aaaa-dda53126c2ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Docket tracking"}], "description": "Observation teaches students to connect textbook procedure to real courtroom practice."}, {"id": "fc42c317-ab28-4b17-bb54-16c943e29be8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Policy reform analysis", "children": [{"id": "3da37847-f4fe-4c0c-bf70-4313b66cd23a", "type": "concept", "title": "Problem definition"}, {"id": "f1480119-a62f-4fdd-9d4c-ae2bb9704659", "type": "concept", "title": "Stakeholder analysis"}, {"id": "3b855ed5-69fa-4ea6-9549-c7d0eada05bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Implementation constraints"}, {"id": "ba587382-e5c7-4918-bab9-75ab749b017a", "type": "concept", "title": "Equity impact"}], "description": "Court study asks what should change and what tradeoffs reform creates."}, {"id": "15ef3a13-e62b-4c7d-80bc-edc6b30513a9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Capstone memo or case study", "children": [{"id": "8ae556ab-4b6f-45c3-84a4-ac68a60ded4e", "type": "concept", "title": "Court profile"}, {"id": "c033b6f1-f674-49af-b6ba-b1f375b5c75f", "type": "concept", "title": "Caseflow analysis"}, {"id": "5fa7a290-d839-42a5-a06b-0a3519cea42d", "type": "concept", "title": "Evidence-based recommendation"}, {"id": "d56c3b23-43a8-4550-b05b-3c96acd82e7a", "type": "concept", "title": "Presentation and reflection"}], "description": "The capstone synthesizes institutional knowledge, data, doctrine, and observation into a professional analysis."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$ctadjson$::jsonb,
