ention, and case management.", "children": [{"id": "f8dd3318-ce1c-4f55-abb7-825a3a0e6ae9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Initial court events", "children": [{"id": "dea12c2a-175d-49d8-b533-47ee204b0edc", "type": "concept", "title": "Arraignment"}, {"id": "5e2ed019-5dd3-4b03-9946-358e8efbca51", "type": "concept", "title": "Initial appearance"}, {"id": "f5b8ea07-bdbd-4976-a52b-065b2f05de0d", "type": "concept", "title": "Probable cause"}, {"id": "f79657dd-8fca-4b92-b0a7-7ffe92a9d036", "type": "concept", "title": "Appointment of counsel"}], "description": "Early hearings set the trajectory for release, counsel, charges, and negotiation."}, {"id": "7ae27d5e-4c11-41a0-bf28-287b345af056", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Bail and pretrial detention", "children": [{"id": "8dc1b80f-d688-4f80-975b-648284473310", "type": "concept", "title": "Cash bail"}, {"id": "b1ef9358-e20d-4fea-915a-3ba8b175f727", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk assessment"}, {"id": "28b94824-1a19-439d-9db3-557f55eaced5", "type": "concept", "title": "Conditions of release"}, {"id": "fde9a218-1c21-4d77-832c-fe7a19eab1cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Preventive detention"}], "description": "Release decisions affect liberty, plea pressure, employment, families, and case outcomes."}, {"id": "16b9f48b-ab61-4988-a029-ccd53e5925cb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pretrial motions and case management", "children": [{"id": "e4010422-1af1-479a-9cdc-02abc8908485", "type": "concept", "title": "Suppression motions"}, {"id": "d117cef4-b01c-4400-8982-071c4145b257", "type": "concept", "title": "Discovery motions"}, {"id": "14cf93bd-506c-40aa-b928-d953d178c204", "type": "concept", "title": "Continuances"}, {"id": "bc7ac1fd-be0c-4024-ae7d-bdecfe051923", "type": "concept", "title": "Speedy trial"}], "description": "Pretrial litigation shapes what issues, evidence, and rights survive into trial or plea."}]}, {"id": "126919fa-3072-4e91-895d-328f174432de", "type": "topic", "title": "Plea Bargaining, Diversion, and Case Disposition", "description": "Learn why most criminal cases end without trial and how negotiated justice affects fairness, efficiency, and legitimacy.", "children": [{"id": "49ce0192-0f21-4d90-aaba-7f8c84f8d931", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Plea bargaining structure", "children": [{"id": "4549a747-37b6-43de-996e-84a1573bcf8a", "type": "concept", "title": "Charge bargains"}, {"id": "45020665-ff41-4e4b-935c-7630ab8df6a5", "type": "concept", "title": "Sentence bargains"}, {"id": "cc58566f-d0ff-42a4-add2-abd5e9b56e49", "type": "concept", "title": "Fact bargaining"}, {"id": "8432ba66-4981-4b28-a342-8d6642daa7eb", "type": "concept", "title": "Judicial role"}], "description": "Plea bargaining is the dominant mode of American criminal adjudication."}, {"id": "5d0a1de3-9b53-4f20-bb6a-fd8d1c39dd32", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Voluntariness and informed choice", "children": [{"id": "dff44008-4c24-41be-a90e-db20a0b4f2ef", "type": "concept", "title": "Rights waived"}, {"id": "f2b6f5ca-17be-4e90-bd1b-cab30c59340a", "type": "concept", "title": "Plea colloquy"}, {"id": "8ab71a6d-f359-4854-a860-e127a39c3c32", "type": "concept", "title": "Immigration consequences"}, {"id": "fc48fee2-26b3-4746-ae6e-9e1ebbe943bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Coercion concerns"}], "description": "A valid plea requires knowing, voluntary, and intelligent waiver of trial rights."}, {"id": "b5f1cf9e-04a6-4a9f-9298-744b5146734e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Diversion and alternatives", "children": [{"id": "d93cf67a-1095-488b-bbe1-4b15ed012f94", "type": "concept", "title": "Deferred prosecution"}, {"id": "ff13db57-bb7e-4d2c-b113-ec3a4439a014", "type": "concept", "title": "Treatment programs"}, {"id": "152e2614-5d15-4f5a-a3f0-f2c6946aeb84", "type": "concept", "title": "Restorative options"}, {"id": "5cd6cbd6-5c88-4cd9-9500-c9a747fef9aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Eligibility criteria"}], "description": "Diversion can reduce punishment and collateral consequences, but access and accountability vary."}]}, {"id": "98640d6c-bd69-4b66-b183-7bcb828d1987", "type": "topic", "title": "Evidence, Discovery, and Case Preparation", "description": "Connect adjudication to the flow of information, disclosure duties, evidentiary rules, and trial readiness.", "children": [{"id": "2c407d30-6424-4c50-a8d9-75e7b3056819", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Discovery obligations", "children": [{"id": "8c8ab7cf-6a66-4465-8ad1-3e7c002ce521", "type": "concept", "title": "Prosecution disclosure"}, {"id": "e72d4bd3-ae98-464f-a388-4dc56a682dda", "type": "concept", "title": "Defense discovery"}, {"id": "605d4a24-b8de-4910-85c5-d5d19a516228", "type": "concept", "title": "Brady material"}, {"id": "03afd993-e83f-4fa8-91b4-3e5f0437baf9", "type": "concept", "title": "Protective orders"}], "description": "Information exchange affects fairness, trial preparation, and plea bargaining."}, {"id": "cb02a799-765d-43c1-aef3-5adb34c1812a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evidence basics", "children": [{"id": "fcb2efb9-2bc8-43d5-b655-ee3287afa709", "type": "concept", "title": "Relevance"}, {"id": "333895ad-9cd2-404f-b6d8-927f4b87ab43", "type": "concept", "title": "Hearsay"}, {"id": "0f9a4e0a-87c7-4b2e-980c-ec1fd9325816", "type": "concept", "title": "Authentication"}, {"id": "c116723f-0836-4d4b-bcce-e1bfc7e081ac", "type": "concept", "title": "Impeachment"}], "description": "Students need practical fluency in relevance, hearsay, authentication, and witness credibility."}, {"id": "11c5b3a2-5d3f-4f59-afd7-eaac58855143", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Case preparation", "children": [{"id": "85f3a564-6456-4b57-b40c-61d73091e76d", "type": "concept", "title": "Witness interviews"}, {"id": "ffe5149f-8977-4627-b9ec-af553f3549f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Exhibit management"}, {"id": "d8cea7b0-26e5-4675-9c9f-243e188a9680", "type": "concept", "title": "Proof charts"}, {"id": "be80df67-129b-494a-9d20-8820cd642d3a", "type": "concept", "title": "Trial readiness conferences"}], "description": "Court outcomes depend on investigation, witness preparation, exhibits, motions, and negotiation strategy."}]}, {"id": "d949ed02-820c-4f85-b07c-86027c2a01e2", "type": "topic", "title": "Trial Process and Adversarial Procedure", "description": "Understand the structure, rights, tactics, and institutional purpose of American criminal trials.", "children": [{"id": "51d71fae-2cbf-4d9e-ac5e-58b14af97c67", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Anatomy of a trial", "children": [{"id": "c08ffdb9-a437-4972-8215-081f1d13b184", "type": "concept", "title": "Opening statements"}, {"id": "65d37b99-133c-4510-be0a-00dd5e4bd7a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Direct examination"}, {"id": "02f34b9f-a56e-4a01-9ff4-22b84e0b2928", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-examination"}, {"id": "a171379f-c01a-440c-a8be-54d07a401b0e", "type": "concept", "title": "Closing arguments"}], "description": "Trial process shows how adversarial proof becomes a public judgment."}, {"id": "74a30620-4568-4d39-819d-5923f23f90e9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Trial rights", "children": [{"id": "7258c310-d4d6-4a36-8d78-862d3a2e7f39", "type": "concept", "title": "Confrontation"}, {"id": "90aac2b8-b431-4f43-87ee-95765b72d377", "type": "concept", "title": "Compulsory process"}, {"id": "23fa15f8-5236-4eee-8b4a-de2d3aaa9a60", "type": "concept", "title": "Right to jury"}, {"id": "c2d918aa-f6fa-4b22-86ef-ff9e1bdde3a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Burden of proof"}], "description": "Criminal trials embody constitutional commitments to confrontation, compulsory process, jury trial, and proof beyond reasonable doubt."}, {"id": "1d72e4de-33b1-4b8e-8481-f83071516608", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Judicial control of trial", "children": [{"id": "07164791-15b1-420f-a5a8-5803ef9be76e", "type": "concept", "title": "Objections"}, {"id": "75c8ebd5-5472-4e11-ac14-41092362b7ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Sidebars"}, {"id": "ddab1f7f-58da-47ff-8cda-51e5cc3125d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Motions for judgment"}, {"id": "b2fafd5d-1683-4547-84bc-3880c26ade3d", "type": "concept", "title": "Jury instructions"}], "description": "Judges manage admissibility, procedure, jury instructions, decorum, and the record."}]}, {"id": "8c7f8adb-7947-4c14-b9d2-973ab17c8752", "type": "topic", "title": "Jury Selection, Deliberation, and Verdicts", "description": "Study juries as democratic factfinders shaped by selection rules, deliberation dynamics, instructions, and verdict forms.", "children": [{"id": "4d3c6646-108c-48dc-9f86-4dc99cc0cfed", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Jury pool and voir dire", "children": [{"id": "6b693ef9-2f70-4fa8-8603-8485f9200bfb", "type": "concept", "title": "Jury source lists"}, {"id": "4f04ba18-c8df-465c-8e72-379b8c39981d", "type": "concept", "title": "Voir dire"}, {"id": "13886f65-7a8f-4ee5-80a1-83ff633ebeac", "type": "concept", "title": "Challenges for cause"}, {"id": "7c5878b8-4389-45ed-9c09-3469e7b2bbf4", "type": "concept", "title": "Peremptory challenges"}], "description": "Jury selection determines who will judge facts and whether bias can be identified."}, {"id": "a9df9c70-a73b-40ee-8dff-7a4cb7565888", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Deliberation and decision-making", "children": [{"id": "03c98047-6f52-4016-99f4-ad63fca869d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Foreperson role"}, {"id": "20e54082-4302-43f2-8f5e-f3004f76da15", "type": "concept", "title": "Unanimity rules"}, {"id": "a8c2e0a4-8dd6-4451-8d66-1fbaa810e978", "type": "concept", "title": "Jury instructions"}, {"id": "9473756e-60dd-4534-8139-d9b95079f1f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Deadlock and Allen charges"}], "description": "Jury deliberation blends law, evidence, group dynamics, memory, and instructions."}, {"id": "290b8544-6b4b-4bb6-a54b-baf5982793f9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Verdicts and legitimacy", "children": [{"id": "b99d2dd2-abec-4168-99d7-28fff492f122", "type": "concept", "title": "General verdicts"}, {"id": "559bf5ee-5a75-47e3-b078-2ee7dd524ab0", "type": "concept", "title": "Special findings awareness"}, {"id": "84475c11-00de-452c-8a51-c5921d36854f", "type": "concept", "title": "Hung juries"}, {"id": "dbabe0ff-78c0-4821-bd9b-d9b5dba41b46", "type": "concept", "title": "Public confidence"}], "description": "Verdicts carry legal force and public meaning, especially in high-stakes criminal cases."}]}, {"id": "3f5e139a-101b-40a4-8a66-87e670e4c8bf", "type": "topic", "title": "Sentencing Law, Guidelines, and Punishment Purposes", "description": "Analyze how courts impose punishment and how law, discretion, risk, and policy shape sentences.", "children": [{"id": "748ab275-055c-4024-a3d4-ca7a093c4d0d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Purposes of punishment", "children": [{"id": "866727c9-9eda-4e38-a119-af83bed642e0", "type": "concept", "title": "Retribution"}, {"id": "e8924874-567a-4def-9812-dd3906195230", "type": "concept", "title": "Deterrence"}, {"id": "f0e7c1bd-6116-4b60-965c-8b0d0e9495d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Incapacitation"}, {"id": "bae1a942-06e0-4721-872c-752999070e11", "type": "concept", "title": "Rehabilitation and restoration"}], "description": "Sentencing reflects contested ideas about what punishment is for."}, {"id": "7c9cfd67-302c-41be-ab88-e2db375b1db1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sentencing structures", "children": [{"id": "bc6d7281-c95d-4d64-baea-366600fba0c1", "type": "concept", "title": "Guidelines"}, {"id": "2aecc836-c7f9-443a-a2c5-4b06ff528582", "type": "concept", "title": "Mandatory minimums"}, {"id": "9137286f-ac11-4c2c-9581-0f331f6a6a1f", "type": "concept", "title": "Presentence reports"}, {"id": "c1d7f8b2-38da-495e-8469-5f94bf811a3e", "type": "concept", "title": "Judicial discretion"}], "description": "American sentencing varies across guidelines, mandatory minimums, discretion, and negotiated outcomes."}, {"id": "42777ba4-e339-46c9-8617-00e7ae95a5b0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Collateral consequences and reentry", "children": [{"id": "95922693-ebcf-4971-9fed-24c5eb424742", "type": "concept", "title": "Fines and fees"}, {"id": "078c1ef8-3455-4cb4-a897-489e8917c3e1", "type"